;;; A relation parameter its activator binds to a nested fact: the program
;;; loads, and the activator reads nothing — regression
;;; `nested-fact-activator` (`corpus/regressions.toml`).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; A rule `r` whose parameter `?R` names the relation of its inner pattern,
;;; `(box (?R b))`, and the activator `(r (a b))`, which binds `?R` to the
;;; nested fact `(a b)`. `(solve :no-search)` states that R is root alone:
;;; what the activator does is root's question.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; A relation is named by a symbol, and a nested fact names none. The
;;; activator is held as the fact it is and activates nothing, so `r` never
;;; fires and root holds no `hit`; R is {∅}. The load says so in a `warning:`
;;; where the activator is written, and the run in another, naming `r` and
;;; the activator (Q-M1e2.18, Q-M1f.1). Every command exits 0.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ───────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The program loaded with the inner pattern an opaque slot, the parameter
;;; unbound, which matched nothing: root held no `hit`, exit 0, and nothing
;;; said why; the same pattern at the top level, `(?R b)`, stopped
;;; compilation with a `CompileError` in the Python IR's spelling (`ein
;;; saturate --dump FILE` and `ein solve FILE` at `f8c10730`, release and
;;; debug). The loader then refused it, exit 1.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answers ────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The answer above: every command loads the program, root holds no `hit`,
;;; and stderr carries the two warnings.
;;;

(relation box Node :why "{?3} is in a box") (relation c Node :why "c holds of {?3}") (relation hit Node :why "{?3} is hit") (relation a Node :why "a holds of {?3}") (relation rel Node :why "rel holds of {?3}") (relation item Node :why "{?3} is an item")
(box (a b)) (box (c (a b))) (not (a b)) (rel a) (item i)
(rule r (?R) :match (box (?R b)) :assert (hit z) :why "({?R} b) is in a box, so z is hit")
(r (a b))
(solve :no-search)
